proof.text:
Let $E=\{\alpha\in\mathbf N^s:0\leq\alpha_i<d_i	ext{ for every }i\}$, a finite set. For every $
u\in\mathbf N^s$, repeatedly substitute the monic relation of step 3 whenever the exponent of $b_i$ is at least $d_i$. Every resulting exponent of that variable is strictly smaller, so induction on the sum of the exponents terminates and gives $b^
u=\sum_{\alpha\in E}e_{
u\alpha}b^\alpha$ with $e_{
u\alpha}\in D$. Only finite sums and products in $D$ occur. This is polynomial reduction, not a claim about infinite series or closedness of a module.
